What values are assigned to the uninitialized elements?
 If you make the list inside your program, the empty spots will have random, unpredictable stuff in them,But if you make the list outside your program
those empty spots will automatically be filled with zeros.

What happens if you specify a size smaller than the number of initial values?
If you tell the computer to make a list that can only hold a certain number of items, and then you try to put more items in it than it can hold,
the computer will give you an error.
